From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:59:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] PartDesign: Body reuses a settled tip copy only while Shape
 holds it (issue 029)

Review fix. After an undo or redo had pasted an older value into the Body's
Shape, the view provider had last rendered that older shape. The next
recompute with the same tip handed the settled copy back to Shape, the view
provider then meshed it anew, and its deflection came from a bounding box read
off the copy's own triangulation (Part::Tools::getBounds), where stock meshes
an untriangulated new copy: a different Body mesh and different stored
triangulations (reviewer probe: 634 vs stock 618 triangles). The settled copy
is now reused only while the Body's Shape is still a partner of it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/PartDesign/App/Body.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Mod/PartDesign/App/Body.cpp b/src/Mod/PartDesign/App/Body.cpp
index d31638d..2da144c 100644
--- a/src/Mod/PartDesign/App/Body.cpp
+++ b/src/Mod/PartDesign/App/Body.cpp
@@ -870,9 +870,14 @@ App::DocumentObjectExecReturn* setTipCopy(Body& body, Part::TopoShape& tipShape,
             recordState(memo.result.getShape(), now);
             double placement[16];
             readTransform(body.Placement.getValue().toMatrix(), placement);
+            // A settled copy is reused only while the Body's Shape still holds it: the view provider then last
+            // rendered this copy and takes its unchanged-shape path. Once Shape holds another shape (an undo or redo
+            // pasted an older value), the view provider would mesh the settled copy anew, and its deflection comes
+            // from a bounding box read off the copy's triangulation, where stock meshes an untriangulated new copy.
             reuse = now.sameAs(memo.madeState)
                 || (body.Visibility.getValue() && now.sameAs(memo.settledState)
-                    && std::memcmp(memo.settledPlacement, placement, sizeof(placement)) == 0);
+                    && std::memcmp(memo.settledPlacement, placement, sizeof(placement)) == 0
+                    && body.Shape.getValue().IsPartner(memo.result.getShape()));
         }
         if (reuse) {
             tipShape = memo.result;
